* Fender "Deluxe" model 5E3 (the 1950s tweed, 12 to 15 W): preamp. Original Fender schematic as printed in
* Reyer Velema's "Fender (Tweed) Deluxe 5E3" report (mennovanderveen.nl, project 2023), values cross-checked with
* robrobinette.com/How_The_5E3_Deluxe_Works.htm.
*
* V1 is a 12AY7: one triode per channel (Bright = upper pair of jacks, with the tone control; Normal = lower pair),
* 100k plate loads, one shared 820 ohm / 25u cathode. Each plate goes through 0.1u to its volume pot, which is wired
* "backwards": the wiper takes the signal, one end of the pot goes to ground and the other end to the common node m
* (V2a's grid), so each volume pot loads the other channel. The Bright channel's pot has the 500p bright cap into the
* tone control (1M pot, 5n to ground): only the Bright channel feeds the 500p, but the 5n shunt is on the shared node, so turning the tone down also darkens the Normal channel. V2a is a 12AX7 (100k, 1k5 / 25u) and drives
* the cathodyne phase inverter in poweramp.net.
*
* Reading notes (change these here, not in code):
*  - Hi jack: the two 68k grid stoppers in parallel (34k); Lo jack: 68k into a divider (68k to ground at the grid)
*    that takes about 6 dB off; the 1M grid leaks stay;
*  - the preamp rail x is B+3 (the 22k + 16u node of the power amp); the drawing prints no voltages.

.nodes x gin in jbh jbl jnh jnl gb gn db dn pb pn k1 xb xn t1 t2 m p2a k2a o

* B+3 (node x): driven from the power amp at run time; 225 V is the standalone default.
V VRAIL x 100 225
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k

* Jacks. SW* are the jack-mode switches (closed 1 ohm / open 1e12), set by the jack modes.
R SWH_B in jbh 1
R RH_B jbh gb 34k
R SWL_B in jbl 1e12
R RL_B jbl gb 68k
R RD_B gb db 68k
R SWD_B db 0 1e12
R RG_B gb 0 1M
R SWH_N in jnh 1e12
R RH_N jnh gn 34k
R SWL_N in jnl 1e12
R RL_N jnl gn 68k
R RD_N gn dn 68k
R SWD_N dn 0 1e12
R RG_N gn 0 1M

* V1, 12AY7: A = Bright, B = Normal.
T V1A gb pb k1 12AY7
R R_PB x pb 100k
T V1B gn pn k1 12AY7
R R_PN x pn 100k
R RK1 k1 0 820
C CK1 k1 0 25u

* Coupling and volume pots: the wiper takes the signal (xb, xn), one end to ground, the other to m.
C C1B pb xb 0.1u
C C1N pn xn 0.1u
R VR_BM xb m 1
R VR_BG xb 0 1
R VR_NM xn m 1
R VR_NG xn 0 1

* Tone: 500p from the Bright signal into the 1M tone pot (wiper = m), 5n from its other end to ground.
C C500 xb t1 500p
R VR_TT t1 m 1
R VR_TB m t2 1
C C5N t2 0 5n

* V2a gain stage.
T V2A m p2a k2a 12AX7
R R_P2A x p2a 100k
R RK2A k2a 0 1k5
C CK2A k2a 0 25u

* Output to the phase inverter (AC coupled).
C C_OUT p2a o 1u
R R_O o 0 1M
